"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a3e773249f76e74b954ba7b5d3c594eb21fa439e87dfb6a97bc4da4276405297","event_uuid":"c414e26f-7303-4008-9c41-5a62736c93b5","position":{"commit_sha":"144d45627315e22bfbd5c52dc927f1b570261e69","position":"1794481925545684001-c414e26f-7303-4008-9c41-5a62736c93b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"d79dc47fb42e53c8f3c175b2768e355da814219f5ca4fd1c511e488d84b514eb","event_uuid":"6253021c-75c2-453a-95ac-b8dee6aa4240","position":{"commit_sha":"a3b83150518a9b9dc676be0513f994bd3ae18b53","position":"1794481979828617417-6253021c-75c2-453a-95ac-b8dee6aa4240"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify evidence (AC5): `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` in worktree engine-switch at commit 4240326388e (the tree pushed as Gerrit 3368 patch set 1), 2026-11-12 01:35-02:28 PST, exit code 0. Lint \"All checks passed!\"; import-convention \"3 passed\"; default tier \"21169 passed, 29 skipped, 19 warnings in 2914.79s\"; integration tier \"218 passed, 2 skipped in 153.86s\". Gerrit 3368: LLM-Review +1 (1 advisory: no test of the dedup key under a CONFIGURED non-default engine), Verified +1 (Actions run 43201180786), 0 unresolved; merged as 4240326388e9de56c67096fee4d4015da1a04f37 at 2026-11-12 03:03 PST.\nAC1-AC2: tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py (8 tests: CLI flag incl. bogus→exit 2; MCP sync incl. bogus→ConfigError with 0 runner calls; async start+poll under both engines with findings.readable and sidecar/status engine; async bogus refused before any job; dedup key resolution; same-engine starts share a job, cross-engine do not; congestion identical on MCP sync, CLI exit 11, and async). AC3: gen_cli_help.py --check and gen_cli_reference.py --check exit 0; test_mcp_tool_surface_golden.py passes. AC4: docs/plan-review-gate.md \"Choosing the engine\".","timestamp":1794481406860315913},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 03:13 PST: CLOSED through the completion-verifier gate at 03:12 PST. Gerrit 3368 merged as 4240326388e. The plan took 3 rounds (r1 BLOCK: missing generated artifacts and pinned tests; r2 PASS, then scope widened for 2 test stand-ins; r3 PASS). The 1 LLM-Review advisory (dedup key under a configured non-default engine) is minor and recorded here. Next: oppressive-prelegal-lobo (production verification), which needs antifungal-amenable-mite closed first.","timestamp":1794481979828617417}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794255928093591001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6bcd076b-97f6-4e24-a57a-42ecd84abc6a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef"},{"link_uuid":"635ea541-b96b-4184-888c-9f0da2d29155","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"79cc-087e-ccee-44f3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate is reached through three surfaces: the CLI (`rebar review-plan`, handler `_review_plan` in `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:300`, parser `build_review_plan` in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py`), the library (`rebar.llm.review_plan`, which already takes `engine` since [rebar:skilled-cepevorous-naga]), and the MCP tools `review_plan` and `review_plan_start` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`). Today only `[verify] plan_review_engine` selects the engine on the CLI and MCP paths, so an operator cannot run one ticket under both engines without editing config, and the MCP dedup key (`_plan_review_variant`, `_mcp_llm.py:88`) ignores the engine: a pipeline start and an agentic start on one ticket would attach to the same job.\n\n## Approach\n\nThread one optional `engine` argument down the existing call chains into `review_plan`. Precedence stays as ADR 0123 fixed it and `plan_review.resolve_plan_review_engine` implements: explicit argument, then `[verify] plan_review_engine`, then `\"pipeline\"`. No new config key or env var.\n\n- **CLI:** `build_review_plan` adds `--engine {pipeline,agentic}` (default None = config), and `_review_plan` passes `engine=args.engine` to `llm.review_plan`. `src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt` is regenerated with `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, and its drift test (`tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`) passes.\n- **MCP:** `review_plan` and `review_plan_start` gain `engine: str | None = None`, and their docstrings name the values (`pipeline`/`agentic`) and the precedence. Each tool resolves the engine ONCE (`resolve_plan_review_engine(engine)` against the server's config) and passes the resolved name to both `_plan_review_variant(ticket_id, source, engine)`, which appends `;engine=<resolved>` to the key, and `_review_plan_body` (new keyword-only `engine: str | None = None`, so positional callers are unchanged), which passes it to `rebar.llm.review_plan`. The dedup key and the engine that runs therefore cannot disagree. Concurrent same-ticket starts under one engine still share a job; a pipeline start and an agentic start are distinct jobs. An explicit unknown value raises `ConfigError` from that resolution, before any job is created or LLM call made. Gate admission (`gate_admission`, ADR 0112) runs inside `review_plan`, so `GATE_CONGESTED` behaves identically for both engines. `verify_completion*` tools are unchanged.\n- **Generated artifacts:** `docs/cli-reference.md` (it embeds the committed help bytes) is regenerated with `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`. The MCP tool-surface golden `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` (it pins each tool's `inputSchema` and description) is regenerated by the command in its test's docstring. `docs/mcp-reference.md` lists only names and first-paragraph summaries, which this change keeps, so it does not change.\n- **Docs:** `docs/plan-review-gate.md` gains a short \"Choosing the engine\" note naming the flag, the MCP parameter and the precedence.\n\nPassing one argument down the existing chain is the least change that gives every surface the switch; the library already has it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py (flag)\n- src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py (pass engine)\n- src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt (regenerated)\n- src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py (tool parameters, body, dedup variant)\n- docs/cli-reference.md (regenerated), docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json (regenerated)\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py (variant key gains `;engine=pipeline`)\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py (`_BlockingReviewPlan` stand-in accepts `engine`), tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py (`_review_plan_body` caller, if its stand-in needs `engine`)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll offline with a counting FakeRunner (agent findings `[]`, so an agentic run PASSes) in a temp repo.\n\n- CLI: `rebar review-plan <id> --engine agentic -o json` returns `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`; without the flag the configured default (pipeline) applies and coverage has no `engine`; `--engine bogus` exits 2 with an argparse error.\n- MCP sync: `review_plan(ticket_id, engine=\"agentic\")` returns a verdict with `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`; `engine=\"bogus\"` raises `ConfigError` with zero runner calls.\n- MCP async: `review_plan_start(..., engine=\"agentic\")`, then polling `gate_status(job_id)` to `passed` with `findings.readable` true. The latest REVIEW_RESULT sidecar carries `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"` and `plan_review_status` reports `certified` with `engine == \"agentic\"`. The same flow under `engine=\"pipeline\"` reaches `findings.readable` too. `review_plan_start(..., engine=\"bogus\")` raises `ConfigError` and creates no job (the gate job index is unchanged).\n- Dedup key: `_plan_review_variant` differs between `\"pipeline\"` and `\"agentic\"`. A `None` argument resolves to the configured default before keying. Two `review_plan_start` calls under one engine, with the first held in flight by a runner that blocks on a `threading.Event`, return one `job_id`; a start under the other engine returns a different one.\n- Congestion: with `gate_admission` refusing (`GateCongestedError`, an `LLMError`), the MCP sync tool returns the same `_structured_llm_failure` payload under both engines, and the CLI exits 11 under both; `review_plan_start` under each engine ends with the same congestion failure on `gate_status`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The CLI flag, the MCP sync parameter and the async start/poll path each run the selected engine, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py`.\n- [x] Different engines get different dedup keys, same-engine starts share a job, and `GATE_CONGESTED` is unchanged, pinned by the same file.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` exit 0, and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_tool_surface_golden.py` passes.\n- [x] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` has a \"Choosing the engine\" note naming the CLI flag, the MCP parameter and the precedence.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py","reason":"--engine flag"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"pass engine"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"tool params, docstrings, dedup variant"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"engine note"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py","reason":"variant key"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py","reason":"stand-in accepts engine"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py","reason":"body caller"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","79cc-087e-ccee-44f3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"6abd1ba5-0ff1-415f-bb7f-94197ae7f51e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0376-8839-dc75-4260","ticket_type":"story","title":"Engine parity across CLI, library and MCP sync/async plan-review surfaces","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1d55f359-bf7d-4f11-b081-fb2689ba0054","734a3b02-6bdc-475f-96d5-77bbbd8600c4","de0bf9ab-3a7e-4fa4-a4c6-3354269c5c48","ee3b71ba-b663-44fd-9f41-96eb8de4ac8f","ca2afbaa-c47f-406b-acae-8191868e6fe1","68a47eda-6473-4c85-80d1-36eb2f70bdae","1765a562-ba51-440e-affd-3aada576243a","e3edfeb8-b9fe-49f3-9a01-3a14070c2f0f","fc3e273e-f0dd-406e-834d-8eede9d20559","7a3135c7-5805-48f7-a382-f0974b71718b","635ea541-b96b-4184-888c-9f0da2d29155","67a7bf09-4ef2-434e-8693-d498d5c81c60","dbc3e59d-a419-4956-93a2-4376a262e900","6abd1ba5-0ff1-415f-bb7f-94197ae7f51e","c414e26f-7303-4008-9c41-5a62736c93b5","6253021c-75c2-453a-95ac-b8dee6aa4240"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794481979828617418,"uuid":"4b44fb64-ecb6-45c0-84bb-cc927909a839"}